<title>USA: Personnel Management names president.</title>
<headline>Personnel Management names president.</headline>
<dateline>GREENWOOD, Ind. 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Personnel Management Inc said Monday that Gary Hentschel, chief operating officer, was also named president, effective July 1.</p>
<p>Don Taylor, who has been president, will remain chief executive officer.</p>
<p>As of July 1, all operational and most administrative departments will report to Hentschel, allowing Taylor to focus on strategic issues directly related to the company's direction and growth, Personnel Management said.</p>
<p>Personnel Management provides staffing services to manufacturers and other businesses through 37 offices in Indiana, Kentucky, Florida and Georgia.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
